rows.en:
"...I agree with {a}, myself."
It was Arai who said it, in a low mutter.
This time, Iwashita glared at Arai.{p}

A girl was standing in front of the door.
"...What the hell? Who are you?"
Shindo eyed her up and down.{p}

When she heard my answer, she smiled happily and ran over to me.
"Good for you.
You're still alive."{p}

"I'll tell you the seventh story.
Before the seventh one comes."
Everyone's eyes turned to her at once.{p}

"The seventh one's coming?
For real?"
Even Shindo seemed interested.{p}

"...If even one person goes home, someone will die for sure.
So you can't go home.
We have to break the curse."{p}

"Hey, {a}.
If you promise to marry me, I'll save you.
I'll tell you the seventh story."{p}

"...All right.
We only just met today, but I feel like this meeting was meant to be.
If you'll have me, I'd be glad to."{p}

"Okay then, I'll tell it."
With that, Motoki settled back into her seat.
Even the bunch who had been laughing a moment ago fell silent, like a receding wave.{p}

...Scary story, huh?
And that's the end of my story.
Thanks for all your hard work.{p}
